Support GTSAM 4.3.0

GTSAM 4.3.0 removed gtsam/base/make_shared.h and gtsam::make_shared
(borglab/gtsam#2579), so glim failed with "make_shared is not a member of
gtsam".

Add glim::make_shared_ptr in glim/util/gtsam_make_shared.hpp. It forwards to
gtsam::make_shared when make_shared.h exists (GTSAM 4.2 and 4.3a1) and to
std::make_shared otherwise. It is not named make_shared to avoid ambiguities
with std::make_shared and boost::make_shared, and it does not depend on any
gtsam_points change.

Tested by building glim against GTSAM 4.2.2, 4.3a1 and 4.3.0, the first two
with the unpatched gtsam_points 1.2.2.

diff --git a/include/glim/util/gtsam_make_shared.hpp b/include/glim/util/gtsam_make_shared.hpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..723d660
--- /dev/null
+++ b/include/glim/util/gtsam_make_shared.hpp
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+#pragma once
+
+#include <memory>
+#include <utility>
+
+#if __has_include(<gtsam/base/make_shared.h>)
+// Removed in GTSAM 4.3.0 (borglab/gtsam#2579), where std::make_shared handles over-aligned types (C++17).
+#include <gtsam/base/make_shared.h>
+#define GLIM_HAS_GTSAM_MAKE_SHARED
+#endif
+
+namespace glim {
+
+/// Allocate an object owned by the smart pointer type used by GTSAM (boost::shared_ptr before 4.3, std::shared_ptr since).
+/// Not named make_shared to avoid ambiguities with std::make_shared and boost::make_shared.
+template <typename T, typename... Args>
+auto make_shared_ptr(Args&&... args) {
+#ifdef GLIM_HAS_GTSAM_MAKE_SHARED
+  return gtsam::make_shared<T>(std::forward<Args>(args)...);
+#else
+  return std::make_shared<T>(std::forward<Args>(args)...);
+#endif
+}
+
+}  // namespace glim
